From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:23:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 46/49] Box hooks for Mur, dispersive materials and the closed
 cylinder

With these every extension of the six benchmark cases and of the board
models has box hooks, so the y-banded fused sweep and the tiled sweep's
box mode cover them.

Mur: face cells sorted by y per x-line; a y-face couples two rows, so
Engine_Extension::GetCoupledRows names the lower row of each pair and
the engine never cuts a band or a thread's y share between them
(SetupYCuts, m_BandEdges). The slow path and unsorted layouts keep the
line hooks.

Conducting sheets, Lorentz, Drude and Debye: the packed groups of up to
four positions of one x-line are found by key range; a group cut by the
y range runs the same group function on a thread-local copy whose
outside lanes repeat an inside lane, and only the inside lanes are
written back. The unpacked and merged paths have box loops with the
same per-position arithmetic.

Closed cylinder (alpha closed): the extension declares Y_WRAP. The last
band runs row 0 as a box of its own first, the first band starts at
row 1, and the block of x-line 0 (r = 0 reads every row) runs in whole
planes. The tiled sweep keeps its hook stages on such a mesh.

Bit-identical to the line hooks: raw fields and probes on 17 kinds of
model (H from 1 to NY-1, 1 to 6 threads, flags, block and balance
variants, packed and merged ADE off), closed cylinder with and without
the axis, steady-state stop step with Mur, the six benchmark cases with
bands of 5, 2 and 1 lines and at 8 M cells with bands of 24.

Mac Studio (M5 Max), upstream bench.py with a source, 30 M cells,
18 threads, automatic bands, MC/s before -> after: antenna 2537 -> 3936,
cylindrical 3901 -> 5797, dispersive 1320 -> 2121; probes identical on
all six cases at 1 M, 8 M and 30 M cells at 6, 12 and 18 threads.

